% -*- mode: LaTeX -*-
%
% [Reaper] Keep Xy-pic / Qcircuit diagrams from destroying the conversion.
%
% `\Qcircuit` is only an alias for Xy-pic's `\xymatrix` (qcircuit.sty:
% `\newcommand{\Qcircuit}{\xymatrix @*=<0em>}`). LaTeXML cannot lay out Xy-pic
% matrices: every `_`/`^` inside a diagram is reported as "Script ... can only
% appear in math mode" (one error per subscript), and the malformed alignment
% then *swallows the rest of the document* — the output simply stops at the
% first diagram. Reproduced with arXiv:2111.05176: sections 8-10, the
% bibliography and all appendices were missing, even though LaTeXML reported a
% completed conversion (Status:conversion:2).
%
% Fix, without touching the paper's sources: override `\xymatrix` so that it
% skips the Xy-pic option tokens and swallows the diagram body, leaving a short
% placeholder. Loaded with `--preload`, so `\AtBeginDocument` runs *after* the
% real packages defined `\xymatrix`, and our definition wins.
%
% Trade-off: Xy-pic diagrams are dropped (LaTeXML cannot render them anyway).
% Disable with `"ar5ivist_xypic_stub": false` in config.json.

\NeedsTeXFormat{LaTeX2e}
\ProvidesPackage{reaper-qcircuit}[2026/10/10 Reaper: neutralize Xy-pic diagrams for LaTeXML]

\makeatletter
% Skip option tokens (`@C=1em`, `@R=.7em`, `@*=<0em>`, `@!R`, ...) until the
% begin-group token, then swallow the braced diagram body.
\def\reaperSkipDiagram{%
  \@ifnextchar\bgroup{\reaperEatDiagram}{\reaperSkipDiagramI}}
\def\reaperSkipDiagramI#1{\reaperSkipDiagram}
\long\def\reaperEatDiagram#1{\mbox{[diagram omitted]}}

\AtBeginDocument{\let\xymatrix\reaperSkipDiagram}
\makeatother
